# Build context excludes. Read alongside the Dockerfile, which COPYs exactly
# two things: backend/requirements*.txt, then all of backend/.
#
# SYNTAX WARNING: this is NOT .gitignore. Docker matches with Go
# filepath.Match semantics, where `*` does not cross `/` and a bare
# `__pycache__` anchors to the context ROOT only. Recursive excludes therefore
# need an explicit `**/` prefix -- writing `__pycache__` here would silently
# exclude nothing.
#
# These are SURGICAL excludes on purpose. An `*`-then-negate allowlist is
# easier to get subtly wrong, and the failure mode is not a broken build: COPY
# succeeds, the image ships, and it dies at runtime in production on the first
# request that needs the missing file.
#
# NEVER add a pattern matching backend/app/pose/models/pose_landmarker_full.task
# (the vendored 9.4 MB BlazePose bundle) or any of backend/app/**. The bundle is
# resolved relative to the package dir and verified by size AND SHA-256 at load,
# so it must be present and byte-exact. In particular: no `*.task`, and no
# `models/` -- `models` is also the name of two live source packages
# (backend/app/models, backend/app/pose/models).

# --- Secrets. The whole reason this file exists. -------------------------
# backend/.env holds real credentials and is gitignored, but gitignore has no
# bearing on the build context: `COPY backend/ ./backend/` would bake it into
# an image layer where it stays readable forever.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- Python caches. Stale bytecode compiled against the host interpreter. -
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache

# --- Not referenced by the Dockerfile's COPYs; context weight only. -------
.git
frontend
docs

# --- Tests. Not imported by app.main; the runtime image never runs them. --
backend/tests

# --- Build output: ~21 MB of debug frame JPEGs and CSVs, no app references.
backend/build

# --- Training/eval footage, ~76 MB total, never read at runtime. ----------
# One of these holds unlicensed broadcast footage that must not enter an image.
tennis_clips*
